<title>INDIA: Indian Oct 24-sector industrial output up 4.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Indian Oct 24-sector industrial output up 4.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's 24-sector industrial production index rose 4.8 percent in October over the same month in 1995, the Industry Ministry said.</p>
<p>    24-SECTOR INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION   Oct 96	Apr-Oct 96</p>
<p>    Coal					 -3.6	    +6.6</p>
<p>    Crude petroleum			  -9.9	   -10.2</p>
<p>    Cement				     +5.1	   +12.2</p>
<p>    Infrastructure industry		+1.2	    +3.0</p>
<p>    Saleable steel			   +1.5	    +3.6</p>
<p>    Electricity generation		 +4.4	    +3.1</p>
<p>    Petroleum refinery products	  +5.9	    +4.5</p>
<p>    Steel ingots			     +6.1	    +5.5</p>
<p>    Nitrogenous fertiliser		 +5.4	    -5.0</p>
<p>    Phosphatic fertiliser		 +12.2	    -6.0</p>
<p>    Saleable pig iron			+0.2	   +18.7</p>
<p>    Aluminium				  +7.2	    -1.4</p>
<p>    Copper cathodes			 +31.9	   -20.2</p>
<p>    Sugar				     -66.0	   +46.8</p>
<p>    Salt					  0.0	    +3.1</p>
<p>    Cloth-mill sector			-2.2	    -4.4</p>
<p>    Cloth-decentralised sector	  +12.1	   +10.9</p>
<p>    Cotton yarn			     +12.7	    +4.5</p>
<p>    Jute manufacturers		     -3.5	   -10.8</p>
<p>    Commercial vehicles		   +21.3	   +13.9</p>
<p>    Cars					+62.2	   +23.0</p>
<p>    Jeeps				     +40.6	   +27.8</p>
<p>    Motor cycles			    +32.3	   +25.8</p>
<p>    Auto rickshaws			  +47.6	   +44.0</p>
<p>    Scooters/mopeds			 +20.6	   +21.1</p>
<p>    OVERALL				    +4.8	    +4.8</p>
<p>Note - The index includes 24 sectors accounting for 50.4 percent of the overall index of industrial production. The figures are preliminary.</p>
</text>
